<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">battlescreen</ansi>

In the web client, a battle opens as a picture: your company on the left,
the enemy on the right, each standing in its 3x3 formation over a backdrop
that matches the ground you fight on. It shows the same battle as the
Combat tab and the story text, drawn for a quick look. The text clients
see no change.

The battle plays out on its own (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>). Nothing you do on this
screen steers it, except the two things you could always do: retreat, and
change the company's focus.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Reading the picture</ansi>

- Row 1, the front, stands nearest the line down the middle; the back rows
  stand further out (<ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>). The three columns are three lanes,
  upper (further) to lower (nearer).
- Each of you shows a health bar, and a letter for your role: F fighter,
  H healer, C caster, G guardian. You wear a small crown.
- Enemy health is shown in five steps, never as numbers: unhurt, scratched,
  wounded, badly wounded, near death. Hover or tap a figure to read its
  name and health, and to see whom it strikes.
- A member who has been promoted (<ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>) is drawn as that
  class, a Paladin in white and brass rather than a plain warrior, and
  hovering names the class.
- A small coloured mark over a figure is a status on it. A bright mark
  means it is chanting a spell. A flash and a number show a blow, a heal,
  or a miss as it lands. A fallen figure lies down.
- In the dark, or against a foe you can't make out, you see one shadow
  instead of the enemy (<ansi fg="command">help light</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Opening and closing</ansi>

  It opens by itself when a battle starts. <ansi fg="yellow">Minimise</ansi> shrinks it to a badge
  in the corner; the battle goes on. Click the badge, or the Combat tab's
  <ansi fg="yellow">Battle screen</ansi> button, to bring it back.
  Untick <ansi fg="yellow">Open automatically</ansi> to keep it shut until you ask.
  When the fight ends it shows the outcome for three seconds, then closes.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Buttons</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Retreat</ansi> sends <ansi fg="command">retreat</ansi>, and the focus buttons send <ansi fg="command">company tactics focus [rule]</ansi>
  (<ansi fg="command">help tactics</ansi>), as the Combat tab's do. <ansi fg="yellow">Help</ansi> opens this page.

Screen readers: the picture is decorative. The Combat tab's Battle view
and the story text carry everything, and are unchanged.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>
